    "doi": "https://doi.org/10.5194/acp-11-557-2011",
    "abstract": "Abstract. As an update to our previous use of the collection 4 Moderate Resolution Imaging Spectroradiometer (MODIS) over-ocean aerosol optical depth (AOD) data, we examined ten years of Terra and eight years of Aqua collection 5 data for its potential usage in aerosol assimilation. Uncertainties in the over-ocean MODIS AOD were studied as functions of observing conditions, such as surface characteristics, aerosol optical properties, and cloud artifacts. Empirical corrections and quality assurance procedures were developed and compared to collection 4 data. After applying these procedures, the Root-Mean-Square-Error (RMSE) in the MODIS Terra and Aqua AOD are reduced by 30% and 10\u201320%, respectively, with respect to AERONET data. Ten years of Terra and eight years of Aqua quality-assured level 3 MODIS over-ocean aerosol products were produced. The newly developed MODIS over-ocean aerosol products will be used in operational aerosol assimilation and aerosol climatology studies, as well as other research based on MODIS products.",
    "field": "Aerosol remote sensing",
    "problem": "The MODIS Collection 5 over-ocean aerosol optical depth product contains biases and uncertainties stemming from retrieval processes, cloud contamination, and surface wind effects, which limit its direct use for high-accuracy aerosol assimilation and forecasting.",
    "method": "This paper proposes a method combining quality assurance filters and empirical corrections, based on relationships with surface wind, cloud fraction, and aerosol properties, to reduce systematic biases and random errors in the MODIS over-ocean aerosol optical depth product.",
    "task": "The task is to analyze uncertainties in the MODIS Collection 5 over-ocean aerosol optical depth product and develop empirical correction and quality assurance procedures to improve its accuracy for use in aerosol assimilation.",
    "model": [
        "NAAPS",
        "NOGAPS"
    ],
